{
  "name": "Maneuvers: Pushing Attack",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon or an Unarmed Strike, you can expend one Superiority Die to attempt to drive the target back. Add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll. If the target is Large or smaller, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 15 feet directly away from you.</p><section id=\"secret-S6d1XbWlRjPp1t0t\" class=\"secret\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature includes a <strong>Strength Save</strong> activity and a <strong>Dexterity Save</strong> activity which will consume a use of your Superiority Die.</p><p>The <strong>Damage</strong> activity allows you to select the type of damage it should deal in the roll dialog.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
